index 0000000..4e04d15
--- /dev/null
+++ b/gpu/GPU3_RESULT.md
@@ -0,0 +1,138 @@
+# gpu-3 (QUEUE gpu-3) — whole-model row-batched determinism, CPU only
+
+Private research (Aefinity-AI/cis2-fp). Extends gpu-2's row-batched
+matmul check (`cis2_matmul_batched_seq`, verified digest-identical to B
+sequential batch=1 calls on *synthetic* data, single matmul, see
+`gpu/test_batch.cpp` / `gpu/kaggle_gpu2/BATCH_INT8_DESIGN.md`) from one
+matmul to the WHOLE model forward pass, on real SmolLM2-135M weights,
+CPU only (host build, `gpu/cis2_host_gcc`, no GPU, no nvcc). Kaggle T4 is
+a follow-on ("gpu-3k"), out of scope here.
+
+Hedged summary: no mismatch was found. This is a useful negative result
+about the specific arithmetic exercised (see "What this does and does not
+prove" below) — it is not evidence about int8/tree-reduction batching,
+which gpu-2 already showed CAN diverge, nor about GPU execution.
+
+## What changed
+
+`gpu/cis2_model.h`: new `Cis2BatchWorkspace` + `cis2_forward_token_batch`
+(§8). Every projection in the forward pass — q/k/v/o, mlp
+gate/up/down, lm_head — is now routed through `cis2_matmul_batched_seq`
+(gpu-2's case-1 row-batch matmul, itself unmodified) instead of the
+per-row `cis2_k_matvec`. Everything that is a REDUCTION in the existing
+batch=1 path (RMSNorm sum-of-squares, softmax max-scan/sequential-sum,
+attention weighted sum) is computed by looping the SAME unmodified
+per-row kernel B times — no shared/fused cross-row reduction was
+introduced anywhere. The KV cache is B independent arrays
+(`kcache[b*n_layers+li]` / `vcache[...]`), never shared across rows.
+Bias-add and the two residual adds are also done in a per-row loop over
+the unmodified elementwise kernels (these are not reductions, so this is
+belt-and-braces, not load-bearing).
+
+`gpu/cis2_host.cpp`: new `--batch B` CLI flag. When set, the program:
+1. builds B rows (see "Prompt derivation" below),
+2. runs all B rows through ONE `cis2_forward_token_batch` forward pass
+   per position (prefill + 16 greedy-decode steps),
+3. for each row, ALSO runs `cis2_run_standalone` — the existing,
+   completely unmodified `cis2_forward_token` batch=1 path, factored out
+   of the pre-existing `main()` body with zero logic change — on that
+   row's own prompt, as the comparison point,
+4. prints both digests per row and a MATCH/MISMATCH verdict, plus row 0's
+   comparison against the pinned `gpu/EXPECTED_DIGESTS.md`
+   `sequential.16` value.
+
+Default behaviour (`--batch` absent, i.e. every existing gate/CI target)
+is byte-for-byte unchanged — the new code is a separate `if (batch_b > 0)`
+branch that returns before the pre-existing code runs.
+
+## Prompt derivation (exact)
+
+Gate prompt ids (`gpu/.gate/ids.txt`, produced by
+`cargo run --release --bin cis2_ref -- --dump-ids`, SmolLM2-135M,
+"Once upon a time"): `[6403, 1980, 253, 655]`.
+
+- Row 0 = `[6403, 1980, 253, 655]` (unmodified).
+- Row `i` (1 ≤ i ≤ B-1) = the same 4 ids with the LAST id replaced by
+  `655 + i`: row 1 = `[..., 656]`, row 2 = `[..., 657]`, ..., row 7 =
+  `[..., 662]`.
+
+All rows are the same length (4 prompt tokens + 16 greedy-decode = 20
+positions), so all B rows share the same position index at every step —
+no padding, no ragged batch, is exercised by this leg.
+
+## PASS/FAIL per B
+
+All three runs: **PASS** (rc=0, no MISMATCH line in any run's output; the
+program itself computes and prints the verdict, this was not
+post-hoc-eyeballed). Full raw output:
+`gpu/.gate/batch_{1,4,8}.out` (stdout) / `batch_{1,4,8}.err` (stderr,
+progress log).
+
+| B | row 0 batched witness digest | vs pinned `sequential.16` | vs standalone batch1 (all rows) | wall clock |
+|---|---|---|---|---|
+| 1 | `d82743059d1db929e710236fe4ec37f89e6f932524801345a006980f7c3cc9df` | MATCH | MATCH | 0:08.76 |
+| 4 | `d82743059d1db929e710236fe4ec37f89e6f932524801345a006980f7c3cc9df` | MATCH | MATCH (rows 0-3) | 0:28.76 |
+| 8 | `d82743059d1db929e710236fe4ec37f89e6f932524801345a006980f7c3cc9df` | MATCH | MATCH (rows 0-7) | 0:53.87 |
+
+Row 0 is identical across all three B values (it is data-independent of
+B by construction — same prompt, same weights, same arithmetic).
+
+Per-row batched vs standalone digests, B=8 (rows 0-3 repeat identically
+at B=1 and B=4 as expected — same computation, no cross-row leakage):
+
+| row | last prompt id | batched == standalone? | witness digest |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| 0 | 655 | MATCH | `d82743059d1db929e710236fe4ec37f89e6f932524801345a006980f7c3cc9df` |
+| 1 | 656 | MATCH | `b34a64b86d50b4f1400ecf05e1355fd1558c733cf9912369e36fa8a8386da80a` |
+| 2 | 657 | MATCH | `42c9dab3646bac3bcfcc82be4ab0fabe77e7bab2d4b2f8920129dd238ca8d707` |
+| 3 | 658 | MATCH | `c01515277ca944815041d1e904a5f19096192b6214f3814e4712f5531b18e501` |
+| 4 | 659 | MATCH | `6147e8feccf9349c5797fd315385c83461ea7f659dddebc65bdd48291082daf0` |
+| 5 | 660 | MATCH | `cdbceaf8822f9bbefdf7172068608fc84771e42a415cf20aa81634ddbc40867b` |
+| 6 | 661 | MATCH | `79bbc2ec3d44066519afe2672fd33651b6332be2e27804b9f585df419064b4ef` |
+| 7 | 662 | MATCH | `b4ac49e22cca1a691d2a0b51cc409afbdff1dc1ee1132a4f2d622d9092a5de63` |
+
+No mismatch was observed at any decode step for any row at any B, so
+there is no "first diverging step" to report.
+
+Wall clock is total process time (prefill + 16 decode steps, batched
+forward + B standalone forward passes for comparison, single-threaded
+host build, `-O2` clang), from `/usr/bin/time -v`; not a timing claim
+about the batched path in isolation (the standalone comparison runs
+dominate — B standalone batch=1 passes are the majority of B=8's 53.87s).
+No performance claim is made here (lab Rule A / no timing figures without
+a dedicated measurement leg); these numbers are reported only to bound
+how long the leg took to run.
+
+## What this does and does not prove
+
+This is CPU-only, same code path (`cis2_dot_seq` via
+`cis2_matmul_batched_seq`) gpu-2 already checked at the single-matmul
+level, now exercised end-to-end: prefill + 16-token greedy decode,
+all 30 layers of SmolLM2-135M (per its `config.json`
+`num_hidden_layers`), real bf16→fp32 widened weights, real RoPE/GQA/RMSNorm/softmax, B
+independent KV caches. No new arithmetic or reduction order was
+introduced relative to what gpu-2 already validated at the matmul level;
+a MATCH here is the expected-a-priori outcome of composing already-proven
+pieces, not a new claim about batching in general. It says nothing about:
+- the grouped/strided-reduction (`cis2_matmul_batched_grouped`, gpu-2
+  case 2, already known to MISMATCH) or int8-quantized (gpu-2 step 4,
+  already known to MISMATCH by design) batched paths run end-to-end —
+  not attempted here;
+- GPU/CUDA execution — this leg is CPU host build only, no nvcc, no T4;
+  that is "gpu-3k", filed as a follow-on, not run here;
+- ragged/padded batches of differing prompt lengths — all rows here are
+  the same length by construction;
+- any other model family (only SmolLM2-135M weights were used here; the
+  Qwen2.5-0.5B GQA/bias path from gpu-2/E18b was not re-exercised in
+  batched form).
+
+## How to reproduce
+
+```
+cd gpu && make host-gcc   # or `make host` for clang
+gpu/cis2_host_gcc --weights-dir <weights_dir> --ids <gate_ids.txt> \
+    --gen-toks 16 --batch 8
+```
+`<gate_ids.txt>` must come from
+`cargo run --release --bin cis2_ref -- --weights-dir <weights_dir> --gen-toks 16 --dump-ids <path>`
+(SmolLM2-135M weights) to reproduce the exact prompt ids/digests above.
