+// SYMMETRIC int8, scale = max(abs(row)) / 127, matching common
+// llama.cpp-style Q8_0 for easy cross-checking. Dequant is done
+// ON-THE-FLY inside the matmul (not on-load to fp32 buffers), per the
+// design doc's explicit preference: on-the-fly is more representative
+// of a real int8 inference path because it changes the actual matmul
+// arithmetic, whereas on-load dequant to fp32 would only exercise I/O.
+//
+// Quantize one row of length k into int8 + a single fp32 scale.
+// q[i] = round(row[i] / scale), clamped to [-127, 127] (symmetric,
+// -128 deliberately unused so the range is exactly symmetric around 0,
+// same convention as Q8_0). scale == 0 (all-zero row) is defined as
+// scale = 1.0f to avoid division by zero; all q[i] are then 0 anyway.
+CIS2_FN inline float cis2_quantize_row_i8(const float *row, int k,
+                                           int8_t *q_out) {
