+# gpu-3k: whole-model row-batched determinism on Kaggle (T4 + CPU host)
+
+Leg: gpu-3k (PRIVATE). Branch: cm/gpu3-batched-full. Date: 2026-09-19.
+Re-runs the gpu-3 experiment (`Cis2BatchWorkspace` / `cis2_forward_token_batch`,
+`cis2_host --batch B`, SmolLM2-135M, 16-token greedy gate, prompt row i =
+[6403, 1980, 253, 655+i]) on a Kaggle kernel with a Tesla T4, using the gpu-2
+overlay-dataset pattern (`kaggle_gpu3/plan.py`, datasets `cis2-e18b-gpu` +
+`gpu3-overlay`). Every digest below is copied from a saved log in
+`kaggle_gpu3/runs/`; nothing is inferred.
+
+## Kernel v1 (overlay v1 = branch @2768a5a, unmodified gpu/ tree)
+
+Log: `runs/gpu3-batched-full.log`. Device reported by nvidia-smi: Tesla T4.
+Both builds succeeded (g++ host; nvcc `-x cu -std=c++17 -O2 -fmad=false
+-ftz=true -prec-div=true -prec-sqrt=true --extended-lambda -DCIS2_CUDA_FTZ=1
+-arch=sm_75`, linked executable).
+
+### Host (g++) binary on the Kaggle CPU: PASS at B=1, 4, 8
+
+| row | prompt last id | batched witness digest | batched == standalone batch-1 |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| 0 | 655 | d82743059d1db929e710236fe4ec37f89e6f932524801345a006980f7c3cc9df | MATCH, and == pinned EXPECTED_DIGESTS sequential.16 |
+| 1 | 656 | b34a64b86d50b4f1400ecf05e1355fd1558c733cf9912369e36fa8a8386da80a | MATCH |
+| 2 | 657 | 42c9dab3646bac3bcfcc82be4ab0fabe77e7bab2d4b2f8920129dd238ca8d707 | MATCH |
+| 3 | 658 | c01515277ca944815041d1e904a5f19096192b6214f3814e4712f5531b18e501 | MATCH |
+| 4–7 | 659–662 | 6147e8fe…, cdbceaf8…, 79bbc2ec…, b4ac49e2… (full values in log) | MATCH |
+
+`==== gpu-3 --batch N: PASS ====` printed for N = 1, 4, 8. This is the gpu-3
+box1 result reproduced on a second, unrelated x86 host (Kaggle CPU): same
+pinned row-0 digest, same per-row digests, batched == standalone for every row.
+
+### CUDA (nvcc) binary on the T4: SIGSEGV before any output, all B
+
+`returncode=-11`, `rows_parsed=0`, ~3 s into each of B=1/4/8. The kernel then
+ERRORed in `plan.py` itself (f-string on a `None` verdict), and its summary
+printed a misleading `host_witness=MISSING... cuda_witness=MISSING... MATCH`
+line. That summary line is a script bug, not a result.
+
+Root cause (read from the source, then fixed and re-run below):
+`cis2_forward_token_batch` called `cis2_matmul_batched_seq` directly from host
+code for all eight projections (q/k/v, o, gate/up, down, lm_head). Under
+`__CUDACC__` the workspace buffers come from `cudaMalloc`, so those host loops
+dereferenced device memory. Every other stage of the batch path
+(embed, rmsnorm, bias, rope, kv store, scores, softmax, weighted sum, add,
+silu) already dispatches through `cis2_for_each`, which is why only the
+matmul was wrong. The batch path had been written and verified CPU-only
+(its own design comment says so); gpu-3k was its initial nvcc compile.
+
+## Fix (this branch, after 2768a5a)
+
+`cis2_model.h`: new `cis2_k_matmul_batched(B, n, k, x, w, out)`.
+- Host build (`CIS2_DEVICE_IS_HOST`): calls `cis2_matmul_batched_seq`
+  literally, so the box1-verified host path is unmodified.
+- Device build: `cis2_for_each(B*n, ...)`, one device thread per (b, j)
+  output, each computing `cis2_dot_seq(x + b*k, w + j*k, k)` -- the same
+  sequential per-element dot as the host loop, just executed on the device.
+The eight call sites inside `cis2_forward_token_batch` now use it.
+`plan.py`: prints the signal name when a binary dies, and no longer formats
+`None` verdicts or prints a MATCH line for missing digests.
+
+Host regression check after the fix (penguin, g++, `--batch 4`, local
+SmolLM2-135M weights; log `runs/2026-09-19-penguin-host-b4-postfix.log`):
+row 0 batched and standalone = d82743059d1db929e710236fe4ec37f89e6f932524801345a006980f7c3cc9df
+(pinned MATCH), rows 1–3 = b34a64b8…, 42c9dab3…, c0151527… (MATCH each),
+`==== gpu-3 --batch 4: PASS ====`. Identical to the Kaggle v1 host digests.
+
+## Kernel v2 (overlay v2 = fixed gpu/ tree)
+
+Kernel `aefinityaiinc/gpu3-batched-full` v2 (private, GPU, no internet), pushed
+2026-09-19 14:29:28Z, COMPLETE ~14:33Z. Overlay dataset `gpu3-overlay` v2 carries
+this branch's full `gpu/` tree; its `cis2_model.h` sha256 is
+`3b409f2f1c6087a7316eb1aac2177a26632d7bcebe30e42125f05450eb833d99`, identical to
+the fixed header committed here. Raw log: `runs/2026-09-19-gpu3k-v2.log` (Kaggle
+JSON), flattened text: `runs/2026-09-19-gpu3k-v2.txt`.
+
+Environment: Tesla T4, CUDA 12.8 (V12.8.93), `-arch=sm_75`.
+
+| step | result |
+|---|---|
+| host build (g++ -O2 -ffp-contract=off -fno-fast-math -msse2 -mfpmath=sse) | OK |
+| cuda build (nvcc linked executable, flags as in section 4 of the log) | OK |
+| HOST `--batch 1` / `4` / `8` | `verdict=PASS returncode=0` each |
+| CUDA `--batch 1` / `4` / `8` | `verdict=PASS returncode=0` each, no SIGSEGV |
+
+Per-row digests, CUDA `--batch 8` (log lines 295-348). Every row is byte-equal to
+the host `--batch 8` row (lines 150-174), to its own standalone batch-1 run
+(`vs_standalone_batch1: MATCH` on every row of every B), and, for row 0, to the
+pinned CPU witness `sequential.16` in `gpu/EXPECTED_DIGESTS.md`.
+
+| row | prompt (last id) | witness digest | argmax digest |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| 0 | 655 | d82743059d1db929e710236fe4ec37f89e6f932524801345a006980f7c3cc9df | 0b9c8f3ac90d0b9cd5f1719ac327dca1fc639fd87468305fccebbe3d56f67aff |
+| 1 | 656 | b34a64b86d50b4f1400ecf05e1355fd1558c733cf9912369e36fa8a8386da80a | b18de42277dc5d36325ea278bf0e1e73ff4b603b850c79255774e30fbc532894 |
+| 2 | 657 | 42c9dab3646bac3bcfcc82be4ab0fabe77e7bab2d4b2f8920129dd238ca8d707 | 8b65037b78b48af1f2f75fd237090c7dcc8f90430d1876441702de21ebad7298 |
+| 3 | 658 | c01515277ca944815041d1e904a5f19096192b6214f3814e4712f5531b18e501 | da6c967fea9082734f43f5e34d7a42eb99e8ea18ce938bb0e8d776f2a78caf36 |
+| 4 | 659 | 6147e8feccf9349c5797fd315385c83461ea7f659dddebc65bdd48291082daf0 | 099198a742c9fc3ccccbe855ddbd56312f05e916d0186b29e0aa1b7ce0d78ee2 |
+| 5 | 660 | cdbceaf8822f9bbefdf7172068608fc84771e42a415cf20aa81634ddbc40867b | 9aabd41c547ebc894194532c76483bfe9b908c9607494bdf223f99d5cb4784b4 |
+| 6 | 661 | 79bbc2ec3d44066519afe2672fd33651b6332be2e27804b9f585df419064b4ef | 807880e1986b5948f0da5b246b8528f9a3955170fedc909c807a5e7773c8d464 |
+| 7 | 662 | b4ac49e22cca1a691d2a0b51cc409afbdff1dc1ee1132a4f2d622d9092a5de63 | 5ebe02b80b4d85ec659a5f7b29a5f1c820760a3439f573458bbd149e4a213f6b |
+
+Rows 0-7 of the pinned digest set are the same eight values the box1 CPU run
+(gpu-3) produced; row 0 matches `EXPECTED_DIGESTS.md` line 12. No pinned value
+was edited.
+
+What this shows: with the `cis2_k_matmul_batched` fix, the whole-model row-batched
+forward pass runs on the T4 device (linked nvcc build, `cis2_index_kernel`
+launches, `CIS2_DEVICE_IS_HOST 0`) and its witness and argmax digests equal the
+CPU host path and the pinned CPU batch-1 witness for B = 1, 4 and 8. It is one
+GPU model, one gate prompt family, one 16-token greedy run; it says nothing about
+other GPUs, larger batches, or other prompts.
+
+No wall-clock timings were recorded by the kernel (no elapsed lines in the log);
+this run is a determinism check, not a speed measurement.
+
+### Known script defect in the v2 summary table (plan.py, fixed after the run)
+
+Section 5 of the v2 log prints `row=N host_witness=MISSING cuda_witness=MISSING
+MISMATCH` and `host==cuda (all rows) = MISMATCH` for every B. That is a bug in
+`plan.py`'s `ROW_DIGEST_RE`: it expected `prompt_tokens=\S+`, but `cis2_host`
+prints `prompt_tokens=[6403, 1980, 253, 655]` with spaces, so no batched row line
+ever matched and every digest was recorded as missing. The raw row lines earlier
+in the same log (quoted above) are the primary evidence and contradict the table.
+The regex is now `prompt_tokens=\[[^\]]*\]`; re-parsing the v2 log text with the
+fixed pattern yields 26 row-digest matches (13 rows x 2 builds). The kernel was
+not rerun; the summary table in `runs/2026-09-19-gpu3k-v2.*` is left as recorded.
+
